As at 31-8-2026:
JavaScript Directory (/js/)
 * ai.js: AI memory manager, player profile habit tracker, archetype weights, and decision engine evaluating Low Power (<5 Chi) vulnerability and Full Power (>14 Chi) threshold bonuses.
 * combat_engine.js: Core combat resolution engine managing turn execution, the 4-tier priority hierarchy (Projectile 4 > Reach 3 > W-Skills 2 > Melee 1), damage calculations, Low/Full Power multipliers, Hard CPU scaling (+10% LP/Dmg), Faint buildup, and damage popups.
 * common.js: Shared helper utilities, math routines, and global state initialization helpers used across multiple scripts.
 * cpu_controller.js: AI decision-making controller interfacing difficulty settings (Easy, Normal, Hard) with real-time charge monitor timings.
 * foresee_engine.js: Multi-turn predictive search engine (supporting 2 to 4-turn Minimax/Expectimax with Alpha-Beta pruning) incorporating W-skill priority 2 execution and character routine (\text{套路}) continuity scoring.
 * game.js: Main game orchestrator and entry point initializing global application states, game modes, and event hooks.
 * item.js: Logic handler for managing item usage, inventory effects, and combat consumables.
 * match_manager.js: Match lifecycle manager handling real-time charge progress monitors, input bindings (W-A-S-D & Touch Pad), round timers, UI control panel visibility, and battle startup.
 * media.js: Video controller managing video preloading, iOS mobile video playback unlocking, center screen transitions, and directional sprite flipping using sourceFacing.
 * simulator.js: Headless batch simulation engine executing full game logic for CPU vs. CPU matches (10 to 100+ runs) to collect empirical win-rate, LP, and round duration analytics.
 * storage.js: Persistence manager handling localStorage reads and writes for saved AI knowledge, match stats, and user preferences.
 * ui.js: DOM UI renderer managing HUD stat updates, LP/Chi progress bar fills, faint meters, floating text popups, and control panel displays.
 * vs_select.js: Character selection screen controller managing Rider selection states, CPU/Human toggles, difficulty parameters, and simulation triggers.
CSS Directory (/css/)
 * style.css: Master stylesheet defining layouts, HUD overlays, Chi/Faint bar tracks, video scaling containers, damage popups, control pad grids, and visual themes.
Data Directory (/data/)
 * items.js: Data dictionary defining available items, attributes, costs, and in-game effects.
 * moves.json: Move set database defining move commands, type classifications, Chi costs, base damage, hit chances, buff/debuff parameters, and video file associations for each Kamen Rider.
 * riders.json: Character roster registry storing tuned base stats (2200–2500 LP), initial orientation (sourceFacing), video folder paths (videoFolder), archetypes, finishers, and active availability flags.

